Analogous to {{sl|en|zh|有|notext=1}}, such as {{sl|en|nan-hbl|有|tr=ū|notext=1}}, {{sl|en|yue|有|tr=jau<sup>5</sup>|notext=1}}, {{sl|en|cmn|有|tr=yǒu|notext=1}}.

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb|indeclinable}}

# {{lb|en|Singlish}} [[have|Have]]; [[there is]] (indicates possession or existence).
#: {{usex|en|'''Got''' problem [[is it]]?}}
#: {{usex|en|'''Got''' ants over here.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=globalise|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|year=2003|passage=Can become taxi driver only. Take home pay, if no [[SARS]] $1,500. If '''got''' SARS less than $300.}}
# {{lb|en|Singlish|auxiliary}} {{n-g|Marks the [[completive]] or [[experiential]] aspect}}.
#: {{usex|en|You '''got''' shower?|'''Have''' you showered?|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|en|I '''got''' ski.|I '''went''' skiing.|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|en|I '''got''' go Taiwan next year.|I’m going to Taiwan next year.|inline=1}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Fiona Chan|newspaper=[[w:The Straits Times|The Sunday Times]]|location=Singapore|page=13|date=22 August 2010|text=You '''got''' send [e-mail] {{l|en|meh|id=interrogative}}? I never receive [[leh#Particle|leh]].}}
# {{lb|en|Singlish|auxiliary|less common}} {{n-g|Marks the [[habitual aspect]] in the present or past tense}}.
#: {{usex|en|I '''got''' cook meals for them.|I cook meals for them; I would cook meals for them (now and then or regularly).|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|en|You '''got''' play badminton?|Do you play badminton?|inline=1}}

